        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Plants: Corydalis\n- Places: Caucasus\n- Concepts: Taxonomic genus\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is classified as a genus in the naming system.\n- Corydalis is a relative of fir.\n- Parnassius nordmanni is a high-altitude butterfly found in the Caucasus.\n- Parnassius nordmanni has blue and red coloration.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on Corydalis species including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.",
