        "original_id": "92043bfa-9225-5794-8fa2-4b00b6cac96f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Genera: Corydalis, Cedrus\n- Species: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Plant families: Papaveraceae, Pinaceae\n- Topics: fir relationships, larval host plants\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is a genus of about 470 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the family Papaveraceae.\n- Corydalis is native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa.\n- Cedrus, commonly called cedar in English, is a genus of coniferous trees in the family Pinaceae.\n- Parnassius nordmanni larvae feed on Corydalis species including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.\n- Firs are most closely related to the genus Cedrus.",
